# Git & docs

- Create commits **only** when the user asks; follow the repo commit style; no `--no-verify` / force-push to `main`.
- **Do not create git branches or worktrees** except the fixed three-lane layout below. Stay on the lane you were assigned. No ad-hoc `git checkout -b`, `git switch -c`, `git branch`, `git worktree add`, or best-of-n / isolated worktree runners unless the user explicitly asks for something outside this map.

**Allowed fixed worktrees (three agent lanes):**

| Path | Branch | Agent lane |
|------|--------|------------|
| `WebSearch/` (repo root worktree) | `feature/websearch` | WebSearch pipeline |
| `../Swarm-Prediction` | `feat/prediction-engine` | Prediction / forecast |
| `../Newsletter` | `feat/newsletter` | Newsletter MVP |

Repo root (`Swarm/`) stays on `integration/all-branches` for integration merges. Do not add, remove, or re-point these worktrees without the user asking.
- Update [`README.md`](../../README.md) when behavior or install steps change.
- Keep persona rules in `Agents/*/AGENTS.md`; Cursor operating rules in `.cursor/AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/rules/`.
- Dependencies: `pyproject.toml` + `uv lock`; respect `[tool.uv]` constraints (e.g. cryptography wheel-only for Jupyter).
